{"name":"Celeste Blue","hex":"#406374","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"celeste","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of celesta (“musical instrument”).","An organ stop, deliberately slightly out of tune to give an undulating sound."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celeste"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Celeste (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Celeste Epiphany Waite, known by the mononym Celeste, is an English singer and songwriter. She began her career in 2014 providing vocals for electronic producers such as Avicii, Tieks and Real Lies, while also self-publishing music onto SoundCloud on the side. She made her solo debut via Lily Allen's vanity label Bank Holiday Records with the EP The Milk & the Honey (2017), and then released her second EP Lately (2019) after signing with Polydor Records in 2018."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Celeste_at_Royal_Variety_Performance_2020_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Celeste_at_Royal_Variety_Performance_2020_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celeste_(singer)","wikidata":"Q76642775"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"},{"title":"Bleu celeste","blocks":[{"text":"Bleu celeste is a rarely occurring and non-standard tincture in heraldry. This tincture is sometimes also called ciel or simply celeste. It is depicted in a lighter shade than the range of shades of the more traditional tincture azure, which is the standard blue used in heraldry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Heraldic_Shield_Bleu-celeste.svg/330px-Heraldic_Shield_Bleu-celeste.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bleu_celeste","wikidata":"Q1055869"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Longridge_Avenue%2C_Saltdean_%28geograph_3002486%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Longridge_Avenue%2C_Saltdean_%28geograph_3002486%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Longridge_Avenue%2C_Saltdean_%28geograph_3002486%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Longridge_Avenue%2C_Saltdean_%28geograph_3002486%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Longridge_Avenue%2C_Saltdean_%28geograph_3002486%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Longridge_Avenue%2C_Saltdean_%28geograph_3002486%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wik